From 9cae2644095f949333f9cd63ffc88dda5e83741a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Casaroli <marco.casaroli@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:39:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fs/fat: Write at the end of the file for each write with
 O_APPEND.

fat_open() moved the file position to the end of the file for O_APPEND,
but fat_write() wrote at the current position.  After an lseek(), a
write with O_APPEND wrote in the middle of the file.  Two descriptors
with O_APPEND each wrote at their own position and overwrote the data
of the other.

POSIX requires that each write() with O_APPEND sets the file offset to
the end of the file before it writes.  fat_write() now does this under
the mount lock, so no other write can change the size in between.

It reads O_APPEND from f_oflags of the file, as tmpfs does, so that
fcntl(F_SETFL) changes it too.  ff_oflags is 8 bits wide and cannot
hold O_APPEND.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Marco Casaroli <marco.casaroli@gmail.com>
---
 fs/fat/fs_fat32.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/fat/fs_fat32.c b/fs/fat/fs_fat32.c
index 747f26898d50e..0092f274167a0 100644
--- a/fs/fat/fs_fat32.c
+++ b/fs/fat/fs_fat32.c
@@ -1436,6 +1436,13 @@ static ssize_t fat_write(FAR struct file *filep, FAR const char *buffer,
       goto errout_with_lock;
     }
 
+  /* With O_APPEND, each write starts at the end of the file */
+
+  if ((filep->f_oflags & O_APPEND) != 0)
+    {
+      filep->f_pos = ff->ff_shared->s_size;
+    }
+
   /* Loop until either (1) all data has been transferred, or (2) an
    * error occurs.  We assume we start with the current sector in
    * cache (ff_currentsector)
